// spec/04-semantics.md: reading a map or file method without a call (for
// example `m.keys`) yields a bound built-in method, and calling that value
// later is equivalent to calling the method directly. Storing the value in
// an instance field and invoking it through the field name (`k.g()`) drives
// the INVOKE opcode's field-shadow arm, not GET_PROPERTY followed by CALL.
//
// Runs against every backend as part of the shared corpus: native, JVM,
// and QBE all lower INVOKE onto this arm.
var m = {"a": 1};
class K {}
var k = K();
k.g = m.keys;
print len(k.g());
